  "result": "I changed `notify` in `src/server/services/notification-service.ts` so it skips any recipient who is the acting user. I didn't run the test suite.\n\nThe cause was that `notify` never compared recipients against `payload.actorId`. When you commented on an issue you were assigned to, the `comment.created` handler put you in the watcher list (author plus assignee) and notified you about your own comment.\n\nThe check sits in `notify`, so it also applies to the other events that carry an actor. Assigning an issue to yourself no longer notifies you, and neither does mentioning yourself in a comment. Events with a null actor, such as `issue.overdue`, are unaffected.",
